   Syst; Int Federat Automat Control, Tech Comm 3 1 Comp Control; Int
   Federat Automat Control, Tech Comm 5 1 Mfg Plant Control; Czech Acad
   Sci, Inst Math; Czech Tech Univ, Czech Inst Informat, Robot \& Cybernet},
Abstract = {We consider a reliable decentralized diagnosis problem for discrete
   event systems in the inference-based framework. This problem requires us
   to synthesize local diagnosers such that the occurrence of any failure
   string is correctly detected within a finite number of steps, even if
   local diagnosis decisions of some local diagnosers are not available. In
   the case of singlelevel inference, the notion of reliable
   1-inference-diagnosability was introduced in the authors' previous work,
   which characterizes the existence of a solution to the reliable
   decentralized diagnosis problem. In this paper, we show how to verify
   reliable 1-inference-diagnosability. Copyright (C) 2022 The Authors.},
