Note = {3rd International Workshop on Knowledge Discovery and Decision
   Making-DECISIONING, Pereira, COLOMBIA, JUN 04-06, 2024},
Organization = {Universidad Tecnologica de Pereira},
Abstract = {The integration of blockchain and artificial intelligence in new public
   management is an area of growing interest within academic communities
   worldwide. This article initiates a discussion on the theories, methods,
   tools, and practices of modeling and reasoning with blockchain,
   artificial intelligence, and new public management through a semantic
   ontology. This paper sets itself apart from related research by
   developing a semantic ontology that extends beyond a mere taxonomy of
   blockchain and artificial intelligence technology usage in the field of
   new public management. It also suggests the adoption of a cooperative
   procedure for future research to build the proposed ontological model.
   Based on the requirements for using blockchain and artificial
   intelligence technologies in new public management, an ontological model
   is constructed. Then, employing the reasoning rules of the ontological
   model, the model is processed through the HERMIT inference engine, which
   identifies the logical relationships among classes, subclasses, and
   individuals to create fields for querying the generated knowledge. In
   this way, the classification and generation of knowledge related to the
   operation of blockchain and artificial intelligence technologies in new
   public management are achieved.},
