   Fort Lauderdale, FL, OCT 03-06, 2018},
Organization = {ACM SIGITE; Assoc Comp Machinery},
Abstract = {Over the past few decades, radio frequency identification (RFID)
   technology has been an important factor in securing products along the
   agri-food supply chain. However, there still exist security
   vulnerabilities when registering products to a specific RFID tag,
   particularly regarding the ease at which tags can be cloned. In this
   paper, a potential attack, labeled the `Hilt Shao attack', is identified
   which could occur during the initial phases of product registration, and
   demonstrate the type of attack using unique identification (UID) and
   changeable unique identification (CUID) tags.},
