   MITRE Corporation},
Abstract = {This paper addresses the need and concepts for an Avionics Virtual
   Integration Platform (AVIP). The scope of the AVIP is to enable
   Integration, Validation and Verification activities like application
   integration, configuration and functional testing. Key of this approach
   is the simulation of the system applications integrated on virtual
   devices at both: On-device and on-platform level using the un-modified
   system function applications that are usually based on the ARINC 653
   standard/API. An avionics platform simulation is setup that consist of
   several virtualised avionics computing modules with the applications
   integrated as well as a completely virtualised I/O using the EUROCAE
   ED247 standard. Using gateway functions, this approach also allows
   interconnecting real hardware (i.e., system equipment or hardware
   modules) in a hybrid setup.},
