Note = {7th International Conference on Computational Intelligence and
   Communication Technologies-CCICT, INDIA, APR 11-12, 2025},
Abstract = {The increasing quantity of sensor networks being used in various
   applications necessitates fair and efficient management of storage
   resources. Because processing and storage resources are stretched to the
   edge of the network in a mist computing environment, equitable storage
   distribution becomes even more crucial. This article explores the use of
   game theory to provide fair storage allocation in sensor networks
   operating under mist computing paradigms. In order to maximize network
   performance and fairness, sensor nodes cooperate to establish storage
   allocation strategies in our cooperative game model of the storage
   distribution problem. Theoretical research and simulations validate the
   effectiveness of the proposed strategy in achieving equitable storage
   distribution while optimizing the overall value of the network.},
