Abstract = {In view of the fact that the magnitude of the first and end of each
   voltage step in the PJVS output sinusoidal stepped wave voltage signal
   no longer has the accuracy and stability of quantum voltage, this paper
   proposes a technical scheme to calibrate the power frequency power
   electrical measurement device based on the quantum voltage stability and
   accuracy of the low-frequency sinusoidal stepped wave voltage output of
   PJVS. Specifically, the average value of enough stable sampling data on
   each step of the low-frequency sinusoidal stepped wave voltage signal
   output by PJVS is used to calibrate the power frequency and small
   voltage signal reflecting the measured power in real time, so as to
   realize the traceability of the voltage and current constituting the
   power frequency AC power to PJVS. This technical solution also provides
   a new way to corroborate the performance of different AC power
   measurement schemes. Both theoretical analysis and experimental results
   show that the calibration scheme proposed in this paper can measure the
   active power with an accuracy of 7 x 10-6 at 1.0L, and has a good
