Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; IEEE Ind Elect Soc; Japan Inst Elect
   Engineers; Mechatron Innovat Lab AS; Assoc German Engineers, Measurement
   \& Automat Control Soc; IEEJ, Ind Applicat Soc},
Abstract = {Robotic surgery performed by teleoperation systems has advantages such
   as support for surgeons, extension of surgeon's abilities, and
   realization of novel minimally invasive surgical procedures. To realize
   safer robotic operation, transmission of haptic sensation is an
   important function for multi degree of freedom (DoF) robots that are
   main elements of teleoperation systems. Besides, large movable range is
   necessary for multi DoF robots, while dexterous and delicate motion are
   required for the end effector of the robots. In this paper, a
   teleoperation system composed of a multi arm robotic platform using
   large circular linear motors and a master-slave haptic forceps robot is
   extended to a double hand haptic teleoperation system. To transmit
   haptic sensation, the system has high backdrivability and position
   accuracy. Besides, remote center of motion mechanisms with large movable
   range and output are realized by the robotic platform. The performance
   of the system is verified by robotic motion with human intervention and
   bilateral teleoperation.},
