   (ICICM), ELECTR NETWORK, OCT 23-25, 2020},
Organization = {IEEE; IEEE Circuits \& Syst Soc; UeSTC; SE Univ},
Abstract = {This article focuses on the design of a system-level verification
   platform for a static random-access memory (SRAM) module. The SRAM
   module is in a CAN-FD SOC chip. The SRAM memory controller verified by
   the verification platform in this paper is an important module
   integrated on the APB SOC chip bus for basic communication with CAN-FD
   IP. By adopting UVM universal verification methodology, a complete
   verification platform and verification environment suitable for the
   module are designed and built; by generating constrained random test
   excitation signals, the function of the controller is fully verified,
   and the results can be automatically compared with the data. The results
   show that the verification platform can greatly reduce the development
   time of verification incentives, simplify the verification process,
   shorten the verification cycle and have good reusability.},
