Note = {2024 International Conference on Intelligent Robotics and Automatic
   Control, Guangzhou, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 29-DEC 01, 2024},
Abstract = {Fault prediction of discrete-event systems (DESs) is to predict the
   fault prior to its occurrence such that effective measures can be taken.
   We investigate the issue of the fault copredictability of stochastic
   DESs (SDESs) in a decentralized setting under dynamic observations. It
   is supposed that the observation of events of the system is not fixed in
   advance. To perform the decentralized prediction of SEDSs, a
   D-coverifier from the given stochastic system with multiple local
   projections is constructed and a necessary and sufficient condition for
   the verification of D-copredictability by the D-coverifier is presented,
   which is polynomial-time complexity.},
