Organization = {Assoc Comp Machinery; ACM SIGAPP; ENSIAS, Coll Engn; Mohammed V Univ;
   Rabat IT Ctr; RIDE; NSF; OCP; Mohammed VI Polytechn Univ; Univ Houston;
   Univ Evry Val Essonne; Mines St Etienne; Al Akhawayn Univ; Environnement
   Ville Soc; CNRS UMR 5600; Univ Lyon},
Abstract = {Nowadays systematic verification is essential because embedded systems
   are involved in processes decisions that affect the life of humans and
   they are subject to several constraints in interaction with dangerous
   processes. To ensure the proper functioning of these systems and reduce
   the degree of failure of an internal part and the time to market, we opt
   for formal method of verification which deals particularly with
   ``Model-Checking{''} model verification by implementing our new
   verification platform SysVerPml that uses protocol models written in
   Promela language (PROcess Meta LAnguage) and integrating generic
   properties in LTL (Linear Temporal Logic) that can be simulated and
   verified by the Spin software and its Ispin GUI to detect all the
   possibilities of error. Until now, there have been few research papers
   directed towards converting SystemC models to Promela language, and
   until today there is no free platform that is dedicated to this
   verification process.},
