Abstract = {Geospatial Information Verification Mid-End Platform for Natural
   Resource Administration is designed in response to issues such as
   repeated development, low scalability, and inconsistent verification
   rules in existing approval and supervision application systems. We first
   discussed the architecture of the middle platform and micro-services and
   also examined the business requirements. Secondly, we presented the
   architecture of the spatial information verification platform. Finally,
   the application method in the construction land approval business is
   introduced. Practical applications proved that the spatial information
   verification platform is highly scalable and maintainable, with reusable
   business components and data services for a variety of government
