Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {The paper deals with the problematics of volume datasets that can be
   considered as the three dimensional regular grids of scalar values or
   regular grids of vectors of scalar values. Volume datasets represent
   significant amount of data located on the secondary storage. It is
   possible to consider related operations as time consuming in such a
   measure in which they cause bad user experience. That is why we proposed
   algorithm that creates metadata in the form of the three dimensional
   binary image from volume dataset. Metadata are able to significantly
   reduce time of important part of the dataset loading from the secondary
   storage into the operating memory of computer. The paper introduces
   designed algorithm and two different Run-Length Encoding (RLE) methods
   in its first part. Evaluation of proposed algorithm along with RLE
   compression methods, using volume datasets obtained by different medical
   imaging techniques including Computed Tomography (CT) and Magnetic
   Resonance Imaging (MRI), takes place in the second part of the paper.},
