Journal = {SUSTAINABLE COMPUTING-INFORMATICS \& SYSTEMS},
Year = {2026},
Volume = {50},
Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {Digitized services are considered as the most valuable services in
   healthcare that make individuals' lives smarter. However, various
   issues, such as security, reliability, massive information retrieval,
   and storage associated with the processing of patients' healthcare
   records, require improving both traditional information processing and
   Blockchain-based systems. To address these challenges, a machine
   learning-based information processing framework and a Blockchain-based
   secure information transfer protocol are employed. This paper proposes
   an improved Wild Geese Optimized Natural Extreme Gradient Boosting
   algorithm for accurate healthcare data classification and prediction.
   This model enhances decision-making by supporting precise treatment
   planning and service recommendations. The investigation includes
   patients' appointment identity, patient details, illness types, and
   disease durations. The hyperparameters of the Natural Extreme Gradient
   Boosting algorithm are optimized using the improved wild geese
   algorithm, thereby preventing the solution from becoming trapped in
   local optima (i.e., suboptimal points where the search halts prematurely
   instead of reaching the best global solution). The developed improved
   wild geese algorithm is formed by integrating the migration and foraging
   behaviors of the wild geese algorithm and the elimination-dispersal
   behaviors of the bacterial foraging algorithm. In the Blockchain
   healthcare framework, users can define access policies and to minimize
   communication delay and overhead, the user data is stored near their
   device location instead of in the cloud. Experimental evaluation
   demonstrates that the proposed model achieves an accuracy of 95 \%, a
   Matthews Correlation Coefficient of 0.598, and a computational time of
   0.925 s.},
