Month = {OCT 15},
Abstract = {The adoption of blockchain in the field of Supply Chain Management (SCM)
   has gained substantial growth in mitigating security and privacy
   challenges for the successful transportation of products between various
   stakeholders. In this paper, a blockchain-based and Internet of Things
   (IoT)-enabled lightweight authentication protocol is proposed to
   overcome various challenges associated with traditional SCM like delay
   in delivery, uncertainty, and different cyber attacks. The novelty of
   the proposed work is established on the basis of both formal and
   informal security analysis, implemented over blockchain-based
   application on a Hyperledger Composer @ 0.20 based on Hyperledger
   Fabric. Formal security analysis is performed using the
   Burrows-Abadi-Needham (BAN) logic as well as using the Automated
   Validation of Internet Security Protocols and Applications (AVISPA).
   Here, informal security analysis shows that the offered scheme is free
   from various cyber-attacks like (spoofing attacks, malicious tampering
   of the product, password sniffing attacks, denial of service attacks,
   direct attacks, compromised server attacks, insider attacks,
